{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. My process involved building a complete source ledger by tracing every limitation in every claim, every numbered part in the numeral list, and every specific structure, relationship, material, and variant described in the specification and figure briefs to an exact affirmative passage in the inventor's disclosure or conversation history. I also checked for internal consistency between the claims, description, and drawing descriptions, and verified that no drafting notes or placeholders remain.\n\nThe review confirms that the draft application is fully supported by the provided source materials. The claims are properly supported by the disclosure, including the dependent claims and the alternative embodiments for a handle, a flexible pulling element, and autonomous movement via stirring elements. The detailed description and summary accurately reflect the invention's structure and function as disclosed. The figure briefs correctly use disclaimers to mark depiction conventions (such as schematic shapes and component layouts) where the inventor did not provide specific geometric details, ensuring the drawings do not add unsupported technical substance. The text is internally consistent, and all numbered parts are used uniformly.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"summary\": \"The complete source ledger was built and verified. Every claim limitation, numbered part, figure brief, drawing description, and technical assertion in the specification was traced to an affirmative statement in the inventor's disclosure or conversation history. The draft is fully supported by the sources and is internally consistent, with no unsupported matter, drafting notes, or placeholders found.\",\n  \"findings\": []\n}\n```"}
